# The hero's armed poses in the shared bank: 11 offsets.
#
# These are the offsets where CAPSULE and CAVES described the same picture
# differently -- CAPSULE "gun aim hold", CAVES "crouch armed" -- which
# hero_pose_consensus.py reported as a conflict and #0120 forbids a tool
# resolving by preference. Two measurements settle it instead:
#
#   pose_height.py  against the 15 committed HERO_WALK_LEFT_BODY frames
#                   (median height 49.0). The disputed offsets are bimodal
#                   with an 11-unit gap: 44.5..45.0 upright, 33.0..33.5
#                   crouched. CV_1784, where both sources already agreed on
#                   CROUCH, lands in the crouched mode and is the control.
#
#   width           16..18 units with the arms in, 35..45.5 with the gun
#                   arm extended. The same split, independently.
#
# So the body posture (upright vs crouched) is measured, and "armed" is what
# both stages' names assert -- the #0120 intersection rather than a winner.
#
# Upright, arms in, both stages assert a weapon.
CV_17CC HERO_STAND_ARMED_LEFT
CV_1664 HERO_STAND_ARMED_RIGHT
# Crouched, arms in, no weapon asserted by either name.
CV_1784 HERO_CROUCH_LEFT
# Crouched, gun arm extended, drawn with the charge indicator below.
# The drawer is CAPSULE_HERO_AIM_HOLD_<dir>_DRAW_LOW_CHARGE_BLINK; the dot is
# a 1x0 degenerate line at bottom -21.5, i.e. at gun height, co-drawn in the
# same frame as the body with no `break` between them.
CV_39A2 HERO_CROUCH_AIM_LEFT
CV_3764 HERO_CROUCH_AIM_RIGHT
CV_5C94 HERO_CROUCH_AIM_LEFT_CHARGE_DOT
CV_5C4C HERO_CROUCH_AIM_RIGHT_CHARGE_DOT
# Crouched, firing. Two frames per direction, drawn in this order by
# HERO_FIRE_SHOT_FACING_<dir>; ascending offset order agrees. The wider frame
# is first -- arm fully extended at the shot, narrower as it recoils.
CV_3ADC HERO_CROUCH_SHOOT_LEFT_F0
CV_3B10 HERO_CROUCH_SHOOT_LEFT_F1
CV_389E HERO_CROUCH_SHOOT_RIGHT_F0
CV_38D2 HERO_CROUCH_SHOOT_RIGHT_F1
